---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Font Finder — Developer-First Typography Tools"
  description="Learn about Font Finder's mission to make font identification transparent, privacy-first, and completely free using open-source Google Fonts."
>
  <article class="py-12 sm:py-20 px-4 sm:px-6 max-w-[1000px] mx-auto">
    <div class="mb-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
        <div class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#ff4d00]"></div>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-[#727272]">01 / MISSION STATEMENT</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-medium text-[#262626] tracking-tight">
        About Font Finder
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base text-[#727272] leading-relaxed">
        Building a cleaner, faster, and more honest way to discover and use open-source web typography.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[#727272]">
      
      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-[#e5e7eb] bg-[#f9f9f9] p-8 shadow-[0_0_0_6px_rgb(249,249,249)]">
        <div class="border-l-2 border-[#ff4d00] pl-3 mb-3">
          <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-[#262626]">
            The Problem with Legacy Font Finders
          </h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Legacy font tools force users through aggressive popup ads, mandatory email signups, paywalled matches, and suggestions for commercial fonts costing hundreds of dollars.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Font Finder operates on a simple principle: when you see typography you love, you need the name, verified open-source Google Fonts alternatives, and copy-ready CSS declarations in seconds.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#e5e7eb] bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#ff4d00]"></span>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-[#262626]">100% Free & Unlimited</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#727272]">No scan limits, no account creation, and zero paywalls.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#e5e7eb] bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#ff4d00]"></span>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-[#262626]">Verified Google Fonts</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#727272]">Every match links to official Google Fonts repositories under the SIL Open Font License.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#e5e7eb] bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#ff4d00]"></span>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-[#262626]">Zero Image Retention</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#727272]">Canvas pixel analysis runs strictly in-memory within your browser tab.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-[#e5e7eb] bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-[#ff4d00]"></span>
            <h3 class="font-semibold text-sm text-[#262626]">Production CSS Blueprints</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-[#727272]">Tested <code>@import</code> and <code>font-family</code> declarations with live specimen testing.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
